  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "86xKx7w9QET6PdZQepDCVAN1WaQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "This records a **documentation bug**, not stack behaviour. Several `03-Build` tutorial pages instruct the reader to generate IDs inside the reducer, and one of them explicitly blesses it as the recommended approach:\n\n- `03-Build/02-DocumentModelCreation/05-ImplementDocumentReducers.md:118` \u2014 *\"Notice that `addTodoItemOperation` uses `generateId()` from `document-model/core` to create a unique ID. This is the recommended pattern \u2014 the ID is generated in the reducer, not passed from the UI.\"* Reducer-side `const id = generateId();` appears at lines 92, 136, 205, 254, 288 and 314.\n- `03-Build/02-DocumentModelCreation/03-SpecifyDocumentOperations.md:46, 51, 150, 206` \u2014 teaches omitting `id` from the operation input because \"the reducer will generate it automatically\".\n- `03-Build/01-ManualTodoTutorial/03-ImplementOperationReducers.md:107, 122` \u2014 same reducer body, with \"We generate a unique ID using `generateId()`\" in the walkthrough.\n- Also `02-SpecifyTheStateSchema.md:39` and `07-ExampleToDoListRepository.md:22`.\n\n`generateId` is non-deterministic. In `packages/shared/document-model/utils.ts` it is:\n\n```typescript\nexport function generateId(method?: \"UUIDv4\"): string {\n  if (method && method.toString() !== \"UUIDv4\") { throw new Error(...); }\n  return globalThis.crypto.randomUUID();\n}\n```\n\nCalling it in a reducer means two peers folding the same operation log produce different IDs, and a document replayed from its own log no longer reproduces its stored state \u2014 the same class of failure as the `initialState` hash mismatch.\n\n**The rest of the docs are right.** `02-Learn/08-deep-dives/01-reducers-in-depth.mdx:13` states \"No time or randomness. No `Date.now()`, no `Math.random()`, no `crypto.randomUUID()` \u2014 those values come from action inputs.\" `02-Learn/03-document-models/03-actions-and-reducers.mdx` shows `generateId()` called **in the editor before dispatch** and includes a quiz answer explaining that random fallbacks make a reducer non-deterministic. The purity rule and the Learn track are correct; the Build tutorial pages are stale legacy.\n\nA corroborating staleness signal on the same pages: the Manual Todo walkthrough still says \"Powerhouse uses Immer.js\" where the stack uses Mutative.\n\nCorrect pattern: put `id: OID!` in the operation input schema, call `generateId()` in the editor, and use `action.input.id` in the reducer.\n\nProvenance: file/line audit of academy `03-Build/**` versus `02-Learn/**` at academy 6.2.2-dev.45, with the `generateId` implementation read from `packages/shared/document-model/utils.ts:4-12`.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
    }
  },
